    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/hjweno_norm_D1_dirichlet_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The COMPOUND match sqrt((D(u,x))^2) fires (priority 10) through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint before any plain first-derivative rule could lower the inner D(u,x), lowering the whole gradient-magnitude term to the rule's makearray (interior HJ-WENO aggregate over [4,5]; six mirror-ghost fixed-value faces at i in {1,2,3,6,7,8}) with the imported interior stencil inlined, the mirror-ghost Dirichlet faces carrying the free names gL, gR and dx, all metaparameters folded, zero apply_expression_template nodes, and zero unlowered rewrite-target ops. gL is homogeneous (0), gR nonzero (1) so the inhomogeneous face term appears in the golden. x0 = 0 and dx = 1/8 spelled with the literal 8 (the import edge binds N before this document's scope; grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm contract). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
